--- !u!114 &296316360
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 296316358}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "<style=H1>Available Actions</style>\n<style=H2>1. Measure the Quantum
    Ship</style>\n\n\n<align=center><sprite name=measure></align>\n\n\n\nBy clicking
    the Mysterious bag, you perform a quantum measurement. The result appears on
    the Measurements Board in the <style=blueColor>format</style>:\n\n<style=blueColor>(cell
    position) - (number of measurements)</style>\n\nExample: <style=blueColor>B3
    \u2014 5</style>\n\nThis means:\n<style=Bullet>The quantum ship was detected
    on this cell</style>\n<style=Bullet>Five measurement results pointed to this
    position</style>\n\n<style=red><b>Important notes about measurements</b>:\nThe
    number of measurements does NOT equal the number of blue squares on that cell.</style>\n\nMeasurements
    are probabilistic:\n<style=Bullet>Cells with higher probability are more likely
    to be measured</style>\n<style=Bullet>But randomness still applies</style>\n<style=Bullet>It
    is possible to repeatedly measure a low-probability cell purely by chance</style>\n\n<style=red><b>Measurement
    balancing</b>:\r\nThe number of measurements performed is automatically balanced
    based on the game settings.</style>\r\n\r\nIt depends on:\r\n<style=Bullet><style=blueColor>N</style>
    \u2014 the grid size (N\xD7N)</style>\r\n<style=Bullet><style=blueColor>P</style>
    \u2014 the total number of probability squares</style>\r\n\r\nThe number of measurements
    <style=blueColor>M</style> is computed using the following formula:\r\n\r\n<align=center><style=blueColor>M
    = 0.08 \xB7 P + 7/N + 1</style></align>\r\n\r\nThis ensures that:\r\n<style=Bullet>On
    small grids, measurements remain meaningful</style>\r\n<style=Bullet>On larger
    grids, measurements scale appropriately</style>\n\n<style=H2>2. Estimating the
    Opponent\u2019s Distribution</style>\n\nInstead of measuring, you can try to
    reconstruct your opponent\u2019s probability distribution.\n\n<align=center><sprite
    name=attack></align>\n\nUse the right mouse button on the grid to place red estimation
    squares. Each red square represents your guess of the opponent\u2019s probability.
    The number displayed on a cell shows how many red squares are stacked there.\n\n<style=Bullet>Left
    mouse button adds estimation squares.</style>\n<style=Bullet>Right mouse button
    removes them.</style>\n<style=Bullet>The counter updates dynamically as you add
    or remove squares.</style>\n<style=Bullet><style=blueColor><b>Hold mechanic:</b>
    Holding the left or right mouse button continuously adds or removes estimation
    squares on the selected cell.</style></style>\r\n\n<style=red><b>Important rule</b>:\nYou
    can place at most the same number of estimation squares as defined in Probability
    Squares in the settings. Their total must again represent exactly 100% probability.</style>\n\n<style=H2>3.
    Attack</style>\n\n<align=center><sprite name=attack_button></align>\n\n\nWhen
    you are confident in your estimation, you may choose to attack.\n\nThe game compares
    your red estimation squares, with your opponent\u2019s original blue probability
    squares. If your estimation for a cell is exactly correct:\n\n<align=center><sprite
    name=guessed></align>\n\nA green square appears on that cell, The number indicates
    how many probability squares were correctly guessed.\n\nA green square means,
    you have perfectly identified the probability of the quantum ship on that cell."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 90b8f61def22698459231b25f6c262b8, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -1438503440582932756, guid: 90b8f61def22698459231b25f6c262b8, type: 2}
